; archetypes/individuation — hold partial readings in relation until a more
; capable working form appears.
;
; Individuation is treated as an iterative engineering protocol: arch-encounter
; what the current frame excludes, hear a counterpart, reconcile the tension,
; and return to the task. It is not a promise of psychological completion.
; The verifier and runtime budgets are the stopping boundary.
(
  (# archetypes/core)
  (# archetypes/rebirth)
  (# archetypes/relations)
  (# archetypes/shadow)
  (# std/canon)
  (# std/committee)
  (# std/dialectic)
  (# std/loops)
  (# std/memory)
  (# std/shape)

  ; (arch-encounter lens worker task) — make an attempt, inspect its excluded
  ; material, and ask the counterpart to make its strongest case.
  ;
  ;   lens     mediator over the readings below. A symbol mediates
  ;            deterministically and fires no model; a prompt costs one call.
  ;   worker   a one-argument caller macro, applied to the material.
  ;   task     forwarded unchanged to arch-shadow-scan.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-encounter
  ;     "Mediate the current frame and what it excludes."
  ;     draft
  ;     "Design the data retention policy.")
  ;
  ; Cost: worker is repeated for the attempt, shadow scan, and counterpart.
  (~ arch-encounter (lens worker task)
    '(-> ([,lens]
          (-> (,worker ,task)
              "State the current working account and the constraint it optimizes.")
          (arch-shadow-scan ,lens (,worker ,task))
          (arch-counterpart ,lens (,worker ,task)))
         "Keep the account, excluded material, and counterpart distinct before reconciling them."))

  ; (arch-reconcile mediator left right task) — compare two one-argument workers
  ; in both directions and ask the mediator for a concrete relation.
  ;
  ;   mediator   mediator over the readings below. A symbol mediates
  ;              deterministically and fires no model; a prompt costs one call.
  ;   left       a one-argument caller macro, applied to the material.
  ;   right      a one-argument caller macro, applied to the material.
  ;   task       the material under examination; read once per branch it
  ;              appears in.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-reconcile
  ;     "Reconcile speed and operational safety."
  ;     product-view
  ;     operator-view
  ;     "Release the new billing service.")
  ;
  ; Cost: both workers are used in both directional readings.
  (~ arch-reconcile (mediator left right task)
    '(-> ([,mediator]
          (-> (,left ,task)
              (,right ,task)
              "What does the right-side constraint reveal about the left-side proposal?")
          (<- (,left ,task)
              (,right ,task)
              "What does the left-side proposal require the right side to change?"))
         "Return one relation that preserves the strongest constraint on each side."))

  ; (arch-individuation-pass lens worker mediator task) — perform one long
  ; arch-encounter/reconciliation pass and convert the result into a changed
  ; working question.
  ;
  ;   lens       forwarded unchanged to arch-encounter.
  ;   worker     forwarded unchanged to arch-encounter.
  ;   mediator   forwarded unchanged to arch-reconcile.
  ;   task       forwarded unchanged to arch-encounter.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-individuation-pass
  ;     "Find the frame's excluded evidence."
  ;     draft
  ;     "Reconcile the useful aim with the omitted cost."
  ;     "Choose an ownership model for the queue.")
  ;
  ; Cost: arch-encounter and arch-reconcile each repeat their worker input; this is a
  ; deliberate pass rather than a single classification prompt.
  (~ arch-individuation-pass (lens worker mediator task)
    '(-> (arch-encounter ,lens ,worker ,task)
         (arch-reconcile ,mediator ,worker ,lens ,task)
         (arch-shadow-integration ,lens ,mediator ,task)
         "State what changed in the relation between the parts, what remains unresolved, and the next observation that would discriminate between them."))

  ; (arch-individuation-cycle lens worker mediator verifier task) — stop at a
  ; std-verified pass or feed the unresolved pass back into another arch-encounter.
  ; verifier must return exactly 0 or 1.
  ;
  ;   lens       forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-pass.
  ;   worker     forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-pass.
  ;   mediator   forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-pass.
  ;   verifier   a one-argument 0/1 judge. std/canon's std-binary wraps an
  ;              ordinary question into that protocol; std/seam's std-gated-by
  ;              makes the verdict mechanical and free.
  ;   task       forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-pass.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-individuation-cycle
  ;     "Find what the current design leaves outside."
  ;     draft
  ;     "Reconcile the design and its operational shadow."
  ;     std-binary
  ;     "Design the handoff between teams.")
  ;
  ; Cost: recursive and intentionally expensive; each rejected round repeats
  ; shadow, counterpart, reconciliation, and integration work.
  (~ arch-individuation-cycle (lens worker mediator verifier task)
    '(% (,verifier (arch-individuation-pass ,lens ,worker ,mediator ,task))
      (-> (arch-rebirth-cycle ,lens ,worker ,verifier ,task)
          "Return the verified relation as an ordinary action with an owner and evidence.")
      (arch-individuation-cycle ,lens ,worker ,mediator ,verifier
        (arch-individuation-pass ,lens ,worker ,mediator ,task))))

  ; (arch-individuate lens worker mediator verifier task) — the compact public
  ; entry point for the full encounter/reconciliation/return cycle.
  ;
  ;   lens       forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-cycle.
  ;   worker     forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-cycle.
  ;   mediator   forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-cycle.
  ;   verifier   forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-cycle.
  ;   task       forwarded unchanged to arch-individuation-cycle.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-individuate
  ;     "Keep excluded evidence visible."
  ;     draft
  ;     "Find a workable relation between competing constraints."
  ;     std-binary
  ;     "Plan the migration from shared to owned databases.")
  ;
  ; Cost: delegates to the recursive cycle; use a strict verifier.
  (~ arch-individuate (lens worker mediator verifier task)
    '(arch-individuation-cycle ,lens ,worker ,mediator ,verifier ,task))

  ; (arch-individuation-panel mediator chair first second third task) — use a
  ; standard chaired panel to make several differentiated readings hear the
  ; same task under one framing. All panel arguments are one-argument macros.
  ;
  ;   mediator   forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;   chair      forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;   first      forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;   second     forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;   third      forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;   task       forwarded unchanged to std-chaired-panel.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-individuation-panel
  ;     "Synthesize the differentiated readings."
  ;     chair
  ;     product-view
  ;     operator-view
  ;     security-view
  ;     "Choose the rollout boundary.")
  ;
  ; Cost: chair and all three panelists run; the chair's answer flows into
  ; the panel through the standard arrow topology.
  (~ arch-individuation-panel (mediator chair first second third task)
    '(std-chaired-panel ,chair ,mediator ,first ,second ,third ,task))

  ; (arch-integrated subject work) — do the work with everything the project
  ; already knows about the subject, and keep what integration produced.
  ;
  ;   subject   the theme, recalled before the work and kept under after it.
  ;   work      a one-argument caller macro.
  ;
  ; Individuation is the one figure in this family that is explicitly about
  ; carrying something forward rather than resolving it in place, and until a
  ; run could keep an answer past its own end there was no way to express that:
  ; every session started from nothing and re-derived the same integration. This
  ; makes the work cumulative — a later run recalls what was integrated rather
  ; than integrating it again.
  ;
  ; Cost: one call. The recall and the keeping are both free.
  ;
  ; Example:
  ;   (arch-integrated the-migration arch-hold-the-tension)
  (~ arch-integrated (subject work)
    '(! (std-grounded ,subject ,work)))
)
